  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"7.3.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: herwig\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://herwig.hepforge.org/downloads/Herwig-${{ version }}.tar.bz2\n    sha256: 2624819d2dff105ba952ea1b5cf12eb6f4926d4951774a41907699e2f567686c\n    patches:\n      - determine-length-of-compiled-in-install-paths-at-run.patch\n      - link-against-an-external-looptools-library.patch\n      - replace-std-random_shuffle-which-is-removed-in-C-17.patch\n      - fix-herwig-config-exit-status-and-use-grep-E.patch\n  # 'make install' runs 'Herwig init' to create the default repository\n  # HerwigDefaults.rpo, which fails if the default PDF sets are not installed.\n  # The PDF sets are only used during the build and are not packaged.\n  - url: https://lhapdfsets.web.cern.ch/current/CT14lo.tar.gz\n    sha256: 5554b2f66027accc3fe38b55b846d5c7c6d771283868187870bf9c86e5c46678\n    target_directory: pdfsets/CT14lo\n  - url: https://lhapdfsets.web.cern.ch/current/CT14nlo.tar.gz\n    sha256: ad62063067e1d73942b1aadcaff2e50a6b2e2d28ad989e8bd3eee5f48e05f18c\n    target_directory: pdfsets/CT14nlo\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  skip:\n    - win\n  script:\n    - export LHAPDF_DATA_PATH=\"${SRC_DIR}/pdfsets\"\n    # libThePEG is installed under lib/ThePEG, which is not on the default rpath\n    - export LDFLAGS=\"${LDFLAGS} -Wl,-rpath,${PREFIX}/lib/ThePEG\"\n    # When GCC vectorizes a loop it converts conditionals to evaluate both branches,\n    # e.g. both sqrt(m2) and -sqrt(-m2) in ThePEG's LorentzVector::m(). The result is\n    # correct, but the unused branch raises a floating point exception, and as\n    # 'Herwig run -d 1' unmasks floating point exceptions the run is killed by SIGFPE.\n    - if: linux\n      then: export CXXFLAGS=\"${CXXFLAGS} -fno-tree-loop-if-convert\"\n\n    # Herwig bundles a modified copy of LoopTools 2.13. Remove its sources so that\n    # only the looptools library can be used, and regenerate the build system\n    # for the patched Looptools/Makefile.am.\n    # Herwig's changes to the removed sources do not affect results, and its C++\n    # interface (Herwig::Looptools) is kept. Results with LoopTools 2.16 agree\n    # with the bundled copy to a relative difference of 1.5e-14.\n    - rm -rf Looptools/{A,B,C,D,E,util}\n    - autoreconf --force --install\n\n    # Get an updated config.sub and config.guess\n    # Herwig sets AC_CONFIG_AUX_DIR([Config]) in configure.ac, so configure looks for them in Config/\n    - cp $BUILD_PREFIX/share/gnuconfig/config.* ./Config\n\n    - ./configure --help\n    - ./configure --prefix=${PREFIX} --with-thepeg=${PREFIX} --with-fastjet=${PREFIX} --with-gsl=${PREFIX} --with-boost=${PREFIX}\n    - make -j${CPU_COUNT}\n    - make install\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler(\"fortran\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler(\"cxx\") }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - make\n    - pkg-config\n    - gnuconfig\n    - autoconf\n    - automake\n    - libtool\n  host:\n    - fastjet-cxx  # pick up global pinning\n    # Provides fastjet-config, which configure uses to find FastJet\n    - fastjet-cxx-devel\n    - gsl\n    - libboost-headers\n    - looptools\n    # Herwig 7.3 is the release series for ThePEG 2.3\n    - thepeg 2.3.*\n  run:\n    - python\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"herwig\", upper_bound=\"x.x\") }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - Herwig\n        - herwig-config\n        - herwig-combinedistributions\n        - herwig-combineruns\n        - herwig-makedistributions\n        - herwig-mergegrids\n        - gosam2herwig\n        - mg2herwig\n        - slha2herwig\n        - ufo2herwig\n      include:\n        - Herwig/API/HerwigAPI.h\n      lib:\n        - Herwig/libHerwigAPI\n      # Use files over lib as lib globs get the platform shared library extension\n      # appended, but the libtool '-module' plugins are named .so on macOS as well\n      files:\n        - lib/Herwig/Herwig.so\n        - lib/Herwig/Hw*.so\n        - share/Herwig/HerwigDefaults.rpo\n        - share/Herwig/LHC.in\n  - script:\n      - Herwig --version\n      # Guard against warnings from the use of the obsolescent egrep\n      - test -z \"$(herwig-config --help 2>&1 > /dev/null)\"\n      - herwig-config --help\n      - herwig-config --prefix\n      - herwig-config --datadir\n      - herwig-config --libdir\n      - herwig-config --includedir\n      - herwig-config --cppflags\n      - herwig-config --ldflags\n      - herwig-config --ldlibs\n\n      # The default PDF sets are not shipped with the package\n      - lhapdf install CT14lo CT14nlo &> /dev/null\n      - Herwig read \"$(herwig-config --datadir)/LHC-Matchbox.in\"\n      - Herwig run LHC-Matchbox.run -N 100\n      # Debug level 1 unmasks floating point exceptions\n      - Herwig run LHC-Matchbox.run -N 100 -d 1\n      # The loop induced Higgs decays of the MSSM use LoopTools\n      - cp \"$(herwig-config --datadir)/CMSSM40.1.1.slha\" .\n      - Herwig read \"$(herwig-config --datadir)/LHC-MSSM.in\"\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://herwig.hepforge.org/\n  summary: 'Multi-purpose particle physics event generator'\n  description: |\n    Herwig provides significantly improved and extended physics capabilities when compared to both its predecessors,\n    HERWIG 6 and Herwig++ 2, while keeping the key model motivations such as coherent parton showers (including\n    angular-ordered and dipole-based evolution), the cluster hadronization model, an eikonal multiple-interaction model,\n    highly flexible BSM capabilities and improved perturbative input using next-to-leading order QCD.\n\n    The default PDF sets used by Herwig are not distributed with the package and need to be installed with\n    `lhapdf install CT14lo CT14nlo`.\n  license: GPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file: COPYING\n  documentation: https://herwig.hepforge.org/doxygen/\n  repository: https://repo.hepforge.org/source/herwighg/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - utk4r-sh\n    - GiacomoXT\n    - vvsagar\n    - AlexanderHeidelbach\n    - conda-forge/hepmc3\n",
